## 📋 Project Overview

This project extends the **xv6-riscv** teaching operating system with three integrated security layers to simulate a secure medical wearable (insulin pump). All security enforcement happens in **Ring 0 (kernel mode)** — user space cannot bypass it.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│           THREE-LAYER SECURITY ARCHITECTURE          │
│                                                     │
│  Layer 1 ─ RBAC          (Phase 1)  [8 marks]       │
│  Layer 2 ─ File Perms    (Phase 2)  [8 marks]       │
│  Layer 3 ─ Audit Log     (Phase 3)  [4 marks]       │
│  Bonus   ─ Test Suite    (Bonus)    [+0.5]          │
│                                                     │
│  Estimated Score:  17 / 20                          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Role Mapping

| Role | UID | Access Level |
|------|-----|-------------|
| `ADMIN` | 0 | Full system access — bypasses all permission checks |
| `PATIENT` | 1 | Read-only access to own records |
| `DOCTOR` | 2 | Read patient records + Read/Write dosage logs |

### Environment

- **OS:** Kali Linux
- **Emulator:** QEMU (qemu-system-riscv64)
- **Architecture:** RISC-V 64-bit
- **Language:** ANSI C (kernel) + Perl (syscall stubs)

---

## ⚙️ Setup & Build

```bash
# Install dependencies
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y \
    build-essential gcc-riscv64-unknown-elf \
    binutils-riscv64-unknown-elf qemu-system-riscv64 git make

# Clone xv6-riscv
git clone https://github.com/mit-pdos/xv6-riscv.git
cd xv6-riscv

# Build and run
make qemu
```

