### `user/sectest.c` — All 12 test function calls in `main()`

![sectest.c](screenshots/37.png)

> **WHAT:** The `sectest` program calls all 12 test functions in sequence: TC01–TC03 test authentication paths, TC04–TC08 test file permission enforcement for all three roles, TC09–TC10 test audit log access control, TC11–TC12 test RBAC privilege restriction.  
> **WHY automated:** Manual testing of 12 scenarios across 3 roles would be error-prone and hard to reproduce. The automated suite provides repeatable, documented proof of each security property — essential for a medical device compliance report.

