## 🔧 Path to 20/20

**Fix 1 — File Initialization (30 min):**  
In `fsinit_security.c`, verify `/patient/records`, `/dosage/insulin.log` etc. exist before calling `secure_path()`. If missing, create them with `create()` first. This fixes TC05, TC06, TC12 → Phase 2 becomes 8/8.

**Fix 2 — Stack Canary Randomization (15 min):**  
In `sys_login()`, replace:
```c
p->stack_canary = 0xDEADBEEFCAFEBABE;
```
With:
```c
p->stack_canary = (uint64)p->pid ^ (uint64)ticks ^ 0xDEADBEEF00000000ULL;
```
This randomizes the canary per session — a genuine security hardening improvement.

---

## 🔒 Security Principles Applied

| Principle | Implementation |
|-----------|---------------|
| **Principle of Least Privilege (PoLP)** | Each role gets minimum access. Patient cannot write logs. Doctor cannot read config. |
| **Defence in Depth** | Three independent layers — if one fails, the others still hold |
| **Ring 0 Enforcement** | All security decisions in kernel mode — user space cannot forge credentials |
| **Non-Repudiation** | Every denied operation logged with pid, uid, syscall name before returning -1 |
| **Single Point of Truth** | `check_permission()` is the only permission check — one fix patches everything |
| **AAA Model** | Authentication (Phase 1) + Authorization (Phase 2) + Accountability (Phase 3) |

---

## ⚠️ Known Limitations

| Weakness | Severity | Production Fix |
|----------|----------|---------------|
| Password visible during login | LOW | Use `termios` to disable echo |
| djb2 hash (not cryptographic) | MEDIUM | Use bcrypt/Argon2 with salt |
| No login rate-limiting | LOW | Exponential backoff after failures |
| Fixed stack canary value | MEDIUM | Randomize per-process at `allocproc()` |
| ASLR not implemented | LOW | Randomize `exec()` load base |
| Audit log lost on reboot | LOW | Async flush to disk via kernel thread |

